      "content": "To improve granularity in your predictive model for urban territories, consider incorporating non-financial and environmental variables that can influence claim frequency in dense metro areas. Some potential features to explore include pedestrian density, traffic noise levels, air quality indexes, crime rates, proximity to public transportation hubs, emergency service response times, and geospatial data on local infrastructure such as highways, bridges, and wetlands. Additionally, you may want to look into variables related to urban planning, zoning regulations, and property density, as well as historical storm patterns, earthquake activity, and flood zones.",
